WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:01.173
(guns firing off)

00:00:01.173 --> 00:00:02.533
- [Voiceover] At the height
of the Second World War,

00:00:02.533 --> 00:00:04.536
the Allied Forces were
planning a secret mission

00:00:04.536 --> 00:00:07.670
to invade Nazi-occupied Sicily.

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:09.115
In order to confuse the Germans,

00:00:09.115 --> 00:00:12.558
they devised an audacious
and utterly bizarre plan,

00:00:12.558 --> 00:00:14.586
a plan which hinged on
the ultimate success

00:00:14.586 --> 00:00:15.503
of one man,

00:00:16.544 --> 00:00:18.794
a man who was already dead.

00:00:22.181 --> 00:00:25.005
On April 30th, 1943, a Spanish fisherman

00:00:25.005 --> 00:00:26.999
discovered the body of a British soldier

00:00:26.999 --> 00:00:28.454
off the coast of Spain.

00:00:28.454 --> 00:00:31.722
The dead soldier had a briefcase
handcuffed to his wrist.

00:00:31.722 --> 00:00:33.354
The Nazis got a hold of the body

00:00:33.354 --> 00:00:35.730
and examined the man and his possessions.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:37.820
What they uncovered astounded them.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:39.291
The dead soldier carried letters

00:00:39.291 --> 00:00:41.056
which described critical details

00:00:41.056 --> 00:00:44.179
of the Allies’ plan to invade Greece.

00:00:44.179 --> 00:00:46.249
Nazi officials, including Hitler himself,

00:00:46.249 --> 00:00:47.938
were convinced they had stumbled upon

00:00:47.938 --> 00:00:51.449
the greatest military intercept
of the Second World War.

00:00:51.449 --> 00:00:53.817
The only issue for the
Nazis was the dead soldier

00:00:53.817 --> 00:00:56.487
and all of the details
outlining the pending invasion

00:00:56.487 --> 00:01:00.605
were a fantastical ruse designed
to foil the German army.

00:01:00.605 --> 00:01:02.085
The idea was conceived by a group

00:01:02.085 --> 00:01:03.453
within British intelligence

00:01:03.453 --> 00:01:04.963
which included Ian Fleming.

00:01:04.963 --> 00:01:08.320
Yep, the guy who wrote James Bond.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.230
To pull it off, the team
had procured the body

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:13.293
of a 34-year old man who
had died the month before.

00:01:13.293 --> 00:01:15.727
They gave the guy a
uniform, a fake passport,

00:01:15.727 --> 00:01:17.600
theater tickets, a
picture of a girlfriend,

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.609
and even loose tobacco
to make him appear real.

00:01:20.609 --> 00:01:22.441
They drove from London to Scotland,

00:01:22.441 --> 00:01:24.592
and they put it on a submarine.

00:01:24.592 --> 00:01:26.115
Two days later, the body was placed

00:01:26.115 --> 00:01:29.275
in the ocean where it was later found.

00:01:29.275 --> 00:01:31.487
Hitler was so convinced that he moved

00:01:31.487 --> 00:01:33.075
the bulk of his forces to Greece

00:01:33.075 --> 00:01:34.950
in preparation for the pending invasion,

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.511
an invasion that never came.

00:01:37.511 --> 00:01:39.336
So when the allies landed in Sicily

00:01:39.336 --> 00:01:41.517
they encountered a whole
lot less resistance,

00:01:41.517 --> 00:01:42.928
occupied Southern Italy,

00:01:42.928 --> 00:01:45.646
and ultimately changed
the course of the war,

00:01:45.646 --> 00:01:48.286
thanks to one dead man and a crazy plan.

00:01:48.286 --> 00:01:51.036
(marching music)

